course: dictionary
lesson: 4921
title: One word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the words next to them. The word immune is one of these. Look at the words that follow it, such as immune to or immune from, to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: Immune to something means not bothered by it. A child who hears the same joke every day may become immune to it, so it no longer makes them laugh. Immune from something means officially free from it, like being immune from punishment.
explain: In science, the immune system is the body's defence against germs. «A sore arm, a slight fever or tiredness for a day or two after a jab is a normal sign the immune system is responding.» The body is getting ready to fight germs.
fact: Immune means protected from an illness, so you cannot easily catch it.
fact: Your body can become immune after it has fought an illness before, or after a vaccine.
fact: The immune system is the body's defence against germs.
fact: Immune to means not affected by something, as in immune to criticism.
fact: Immune from means officially free from something, as in immune from punishment.
exercise: «Thanks to her vaccine, Maya is immune to the illness.» What does immune mean here? | Lost in the hospital | Ill with the illness right now | *Protected from the illness, so she cannot easily catch it | Sad about the illness
exercise: Sam has heard the same silly joke ten times and no longer laughs. He says, «I'm immune to it now.» What does he mean? | He has been officially excused from jokes | *He is not bothered by it any more | He is protected from getting ill | He is very cold
exercise: «Hay fever is an allergy to pollen; histamine released by the immune system causes sneezing.» Find and copy the two words that name the body's defence against germs. | pollen | *immune system | hay fever | histamine
test: Which phrase means officially free from punishment? | immune hungry | immune to punishment | immune system | *immune from punishment
test: «Contact with nature and many kinds of microbes may help a child's immune system develop, though scientists are still studying the details.» What does this tell you? | Scientists have finished and know everything | *Scientists are still learning, so not every answer is known yet | Children never get ill | Microbes are always harmful
exam: Why does a vaccine help a person? | *To help the body become immune so it can fight an illness | To make the body hungry | To make a sore arm last all day | To stop all sneezing forever
